## Answer
# * A packet whose section A does NOT depend on a history ref: verify PASSES before and after the history ref moves
#   (verify ignores history entirely: pinned_view_from_manifest builds ResolvedView(history=[])). 
# * A packet whose section A DOES resolve through a history fallback: compile says status OK and places the item at the
#   history commit, but packet verify FAILS IMMEDIATELY (no ref moved) -- history=[] makes the re-derivation see the path as
#   ABSENT, and the manifest's 'view' rows record no history commit at all, so no verifier could pin it. After the move it
#   still fails. -> INT-D05 (owner R1-RM). Not re-derivable; the compiler also emits a packet its own verifier rejects (5.3 r.4).
# * Separately, a records-partition path absent at records is BLOCKED rather than resolved through its declared fallback
#   chain, because classify_occurrence returns CANONICAL (blob None) whenever the queried commit IS the owner commit and the
#   resolver always queries the records commit -> INT-D06 (latent; loud BLOCKED, not silent).
# * Real view today: no current section-A item resolves through history (R1-RM's own probe; CONTROL-A A = contract_v3 at the
#   product/records named refs, see int-04), so both are LATENT for run-2 unless a mandatory input lands on a history-only path.
